hadiths[6]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16593","He said: Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Ibn Mubarak narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Mahmud ibn al-Rabi, from Itban ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed Duha, and we greeted when he greeted, and that he, meaning he prayed with them in a mosque near them."
"16594","He said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, so Sufyan was asked from whom, he said: He is Mahmud, if Allah wills, that Itban ibn Malik was a man blind of sight, and that he mentioned to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, staying back from prayer, he said: Do you hear the call, he said: Yes, he said: So he did not permit him."
"16595","He said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Husayn informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Mahmud ibn al-Rabi, or al-Rabi ibn Mahmud, Yazid doubted, from Itban ibn Malik, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: Indeed I am a man blind of sight, and between me and you is this valley and darkness, and I asked him to come and pray in my house, so I would take his prayer place as a prayer place, so he promised me to do it, so he came, he and Abu Bakr and Umar, and the Ansar heard of him, so they came to him, and a man of them called Malik ibn al-Dukhshun stayed back, and he was suspected of hypocrisy, so they detained them over food, and they discussed among them, and said: He did not stay back from us, though he knew that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, visited us, except for his hypocrisy, while the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was praying, so when he finished, he said: Woe to him, did he not testify that there is no god but Allah, sincerely by it, for indeed Allah Almighty has forbidden the Fire upon whoever testifies by it."
"16596","He said: Abd al-Ala ibn Abd al-Ala narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Mahmud ibn al-Rabi, from Itban ibn Malik, that he said: O Messenger of Allah, indeed torrents come between me and the mosque of my people, so I love that you come to me and pray in a place in my house I take as a mosque, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: We shall do it, he said: So when the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, awoke in the morning, he went to Abu Bakr and took him along, so when the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered, he said: Where do you want, so I pointed to him to a side of the house, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: So we lined behind him and he prayed with us two rakahs, and we detained him over khazir we made, and the people of the house, meaning the people of the village, heard, so they kept coming, and the house filled, so a man of the people said: Where is Malik ibn al-Dukhshum, so a man said: That is of the hypocrites, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not say it, he says: There is no god but Allah, seeking by it the Face of Allah, he said: As for us, we see his face and his speech toward the hypocrites, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not say it, he says: There is no god but Allah, seeking by that the Face of Allah, so a man of the people said: Yes indeed, O Messenger of Allah, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: If a servant meets the Day of Resurrection saying: There is no god but Allah, seeking by that the Face of Allah, except he is forbidden upon the Fire, so Mahmud said: So I narrated that to people among whom was Abu Ayyub, he said: I do not think the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said this, he said: So I said: If I return while Itban is alive, I shall ask him, so I came and he was blind, and he was the imam of his people, so I asked him, and he narrated to me as he narrated to me the first time, and Itban was a Badri, he said:"
"16597","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Mahmud ibn al-Rabi, from Itban ibn Malik, he said: I came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: Indeed I have lost my sight, then he mentioned its meaning, except that he said: Malik ibn al-Dukhshun, and perhaps he said: al-Dukhayshin, and he said: He is forbidden upon the Fire, and he did not say: He was a Badri."
"16598","He said: Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Jarir, meaning Ibn Hazim, narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd ibn Judan, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Anas ibn Malik narrated to me, he said: My father came from Syria as a delegate, and I was with him, so we met Mahmud ibn al-Rabi, and he narrated to my father a hadith from Itban ibn Malik, my father said: O my son, memorize this hadith, for indeed it is of the treasures of hadith, so when we finished, we left to Madinah, and we asked about him, and behold he was alive, and behold an old blind man, he said: So we asked him about the hadith, so he said: Yes, my sight went during the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so I said: O Messenger of Allah, my sight has gone and I cannot pray behind you, so if you would assign in my house a mosque, I would pray in it, I would take it as a prayer place, he said: Yes, for indeed I am coming to you tomorrow, he said: So when he prayed the next day, he turned to him and stood until he came to him, and said: O Itban, where do you love that I assign for you, so he described a place to him, so he assigned for him and prayed therein, then he detained, or sat, and those around us of the Ansar heard, so they came until the house filled upon us, so they mentioned the hypocrites and what they meet of their harm and evil, until they made their affair to a man of them called Malik ibn al-Dukhshum, and they said of his condition and of his condition, while the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was silent, so when they increased, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Does he not testify that there is no god but Allah, so when it was the third time, they said: Indeed he says it, he said: By the One who sent me with the truth, if he said it truthfully from his heart, the Fire will never eat him, they said: So they never rejoiced in anything as their rejoicing in what he said."
